  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best (config_031: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted; 0.678 acc) shows that image features do carry complementary signal when properly fused, but ResNet50's standalone performance was very weak (0.208). The key remaining uncertainty is whether a stronger, more expressive image encoder (ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L) can extract meaningfully more complementary visual signal beyond what ResNet50 captures. Config_037 changes exactly one variable (image encoder: resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l) while holding the proven optimal settings constant (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion), making the result cleanly attributable to encoder quality. This is the highest-value next experiment because: (1) the fusion axis is confirmed productive (weighted >> concat), so a better image representation should yield larger gains; (2) the aggregation axis is near-ceiling (avgpool ≈ transformer), so no need to revisit it; (3) the RNA encoder is settled (scvi_n200 >> scgpt); and (4) this directly tests whether further investment in the image modality is justified or whether the ~0.678 level is near the practical ceiling for this task."
}

